course: dictionary
lesson: 5575
title: Lettuce in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Lettuce is a plant with large green leaves that people eat raw, mostly in salads and sandwiches. The context clue «lettuce and spinach are leaves» shows that lettuce is a leafy vegetable, not a root or a seed.
explain: Context can also show a surprising meaning. In the knock-knock joke, «"Lettuce in" sounds like "let us in"», so the word is playing with sounds. The joke is the clue: no one is eating anything here.
explain: Other sentences use lettuce in new ways. Guinea pigs hear the fridge door and whistle because they know it means lettuce and peppers, which is food. Slugs nibble holes in lettuce at night, so lettuce is food for them too.
fact: Lettuce is a plant with large green leaves that people eat raw.
fact: «A head of lettuce» means one whole lettuce, and «lettuce leaves» means the leaves of the plant.
fact: Lettuce is a leaf, as in «lettuce and spinach are leaves».
fact: Wash lettuce before eating to remove dirt.
fact: Lettuce grows quickly from seed and needs water and light.
exercise: What is a lettuce? | A small wild animal that lives in a burrow | A type of hot drink | A metal tool for digging | *A plant with large green leaves that people eat raw
exercise: Which group is lettuce in, according to «lettuce and spinach are leaves»? | *Leaves | Seeds | Roots | Flowers
exercise: Why should you wash lettuce before eating it? | *To remove dirt | To make it grow faster | To make it smell nice | To make it softer for guinea pigs
test: In the knock-knock joke, why does «Lettuce in» sound funny? | It is a joke about a lion | *It sounds like "let us in" | It is about slugs at night | It means a big salad
test: Which sentence shows lettuce as food for a pet? | Slugs glide on their slime in the dark | Carrots and beetroot are roots | A bumblebee hums on a tomato flower | *Guinea pigs whistle at the fridge because they know it holds lettuce
exam: Which phrase means one whole lettuce? | A lion dance | *A head of lettuce | Lettuce in | Lettuce leaves
